From: Grant McNaught <1371263+gmcnaught@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:37:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/36] fix(render): keep bgplane's full-frame COPY latch
 running before animated ops

The static/animated reorder (previous commit) fixed parallax paint order for
the common case (per-bucket static replay), but broke the SOLARUS_BGPLANE
path: that renderer's resident_emit_static_layer is a one-shot, full-frame
opaque COPY of a plane that flattens EVERY layer's statics into one image,
latched to fire only once, on whichever layer draws first each frame. With
static now called after animated ops, that COPY fired right after the first
layer's animated tiles were drawn -- and immediately overwrote them, since
it's an opaque full-screen blit.

Add Renderer::resident_static_before_animated() (default false, matching the
new order) so a renderer whose 'static layer' emission is really a global,
must-run-first side effect can opt back into the old timing without
regressing the per-bucket case. MisterBlitterRenderer overrides it to return
true only while the flattened plane is actually what's about to draw
(bgplane_enabled && bg_plane_valid); the per-bucket fallback keeps the new,
order-independent-safe timing.

Does not fix the pre-existing bgplane cross-layer bug (still opt-in,
default OFF) -- only stops it from also erasing that frame's first-layer
animated tiles, a regression introduced by the ordering fix.
---
 include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/entities/Entities.cpp           | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h b/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h
index 4bb470f..3f84be5 100644
--- a/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h
+++ b/include/solarus/graphics/Renderer.h
@@ -125,6 +125,18 @@ public:
   // renderer with no plane support (or the default no-op Renderer) simply draws
   // nothing here, matching the old per-op accessors' zero-count default.
   virtual void resident_emit_static_layer(int /*layer*/) {}
+  // [Phase 3b] Where does resident_emit_static_layer belong relative to this layer's
+  // animated op loop? A per-op static replay (the common case) only ever contains
+  // tiles that don't overlap any animated tile's square, so it's order-independent
+  // and the engine puts it AFTER (false here) so animated content -- including a
+  // scroll_ratio!=1 background pattern -- isn't hidden behind ground it should show
+  // through. A single-plane bake that flattens EVERY layer's statics into one image
+  // and fires its one-shot full-frame COPY on whichever layer is drawn first (see
+  // MisterBlitterRenderer::resident_emit_static_layer) instead needs to run BEFORE
+  // any animated/entity draws of ANY layer this frame, exactly like it always did --
+  // otherwise that opaque COPY wipes out the first layer's own just-drawn animated
+  // tiles. Override to return true while such a plane is active.
+  virtual bool resident_static_before_animated() const { return false; }
 
   /**
    * @brief clear a surface
